blocks.en:
Figure 2: Overview of the MEGA framework. Given a pretrained 3DGS scene, MEGA proceeds as follows:
(a) the user interactively selects a target object;
(b) the spatial configuration is initialized from the user input;
(c) the online segmentation module identifies the target object and estimates its position, 6-DoF pose, and appropriate observation distance; and
(d) spatial viewpoints are sampled around the object to generate sufficient camera–view pairs, which can optionally be refined using SAM2.
These camera–view pairs subsequently serve as teacher signals for either distilling an object-level mesh or refining boundary artifacts in the object-level 3DGS representation.

blocks.zh:
图2:多边环境协定框架概览。 由于3DGS场景经过预训,MEGA的进球如下:
(a) 用户交互选择目标对象;
(b) 从用户输入中初始化空间配置;
(c) 在线分区模块确定目标物体并估计其位置、6-DoF位置和适当的观测距离;
(d) 对物体周围的空间角度进行取样,以产生足够的相机-视图对子,可选用SAM2进行精制.
这些相机-视线对随后作为教师信号,用于在3DGS级显示器中蒸馏一个物体级网格或精炼边界文物。
